{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the incense that you shall make.</b> It may be explained according to the words of the Sages, whose memory is for blessing (Keritot 6a), who said: each day he would prepare it in its prescribed formula and bring it in. And this is what the verse says — <b>and the incense that you shall make</b> — meaning: anything that is in the category of the making of the House of YHWH — in its formula you shall not make. From this you learn that one who compounds half a maneh is liable to karet." "<b>You shall not make.</b> Meaning, even without intending to smell it, it is forbidden by a negative commandment; but karet applies specifically to smelling. Therefore Scripture did not stipulate smelling in this verse, but only in the verse where it mentioned the punishment of karet (Exodus 30:38)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:46.197846535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}